cartridge "GRAVITRON/CHARLES ORCUTT/1989"
' GRAVITRON - ColecoVision port of "Gravitron" by Charles Orcutt (graphics
' by Dan Diamante), RUN magazine's ReRUN 1989 Special Issue, C64 machine
' language (+GRAV ML, +GRAV CHARS). Rules from the disassembly
' (c64/ml.dis); the C64 addresses are named in the comments.
'
' The game: hostile ships steal Earth's water. Your ship hangs over a
' cloud field that scrolls in eight directions; stick left/right turns it
' (16 headings), up is thrust, down climbs against gravity. Low (green)
' you can shoot the enemy saucer, refuel at the F depot and be hit; high
' (white) you are safe but harmless; the ground is fatal. Three saucers a
' level; every 4th level a red orb roams, every 3rd a gravity ring pulls.
'
' Coordinates: every rule keeps the C64 sprite coordinates (X 0-511,
' Y 0-255, the 512 x 256 sprite torus); only drawing maps them (x * 0.7,
' y - 42). Collisions use the C64 sprite pixels (MaskData).
'
' Video: title and pages use the standard Amy mode 2 layout. Play uses
' one shared 2K pattern table and one 2K colour table (R4 = 0, R3 = $9F),
' which frees $0800-$17FF and $2800-$37FF for the 120 x 50 cloud map, and
' two name tables ($1800 shown / $1C00 drawn) swapped after a redraw.

